sequenceDiagram
    participant T as Transaction
    participant WAL as WAL Writer
    participant BUF as WAL Buffers
    participant WS as WalSender
    participant NET as Network

    Note over T,NET: Primary Side WAL Generation to Transmission Flow

    %% WAL Record Generation Phase
    T->>+WAL: XLogInsert(rmid, info)
    Note right of WAL: Begin WAL record insertion

    WAL->>WAL: XLogBeginInsert()
    Note right of WAL: Initialize insertion context

    WAL->>WAL: XLogRegisterData(data, len)
    Note right of WAL: Register record data components

    WAL->>WAL: XLogRecordAssemble()
    Note right of WAL: Assemble complete record chain

    WAL->>+BUF: XLogInsertRecord(rdt, fpw_lsn, flags)
    Note right of BUF: Core insertion with buffer management

    BUF->>BUF: WALInsertLock acquisition
    Note right of BUF: Exclusive lock for insertion

    BUF->>BUF: Copy data to WAL buffers
    Note right of BUF: Atomic data copying

    BUF->>BUF: WALInsertLock release

    BUF-->>-WAL: Return EndRecPtr
    WAL-->>-T: Return WAL LSN

    %% WAL Persistence Phase
    T->>+WAL: XLogFlush(EndRecPtr)
    Note right of WAL: Ensure durability

    WAL->>WAL: XLogWrite(WriteRqst)
    Note right of WAL: Write buffers to disk

    WAL->>WAL: issue_xlog_fsync()
    Note right of WAL: Force sync to storage

    WAL->>WAL: Update LogwrtResult
    Note right of WAL: Update shared write position

    WAL-->>-T: Confirm durability

    %% WalSender Wakeup and Transmission
    WAL->>+WS: WalSndWakeup()
    Note right of WS: Signal new WAL available

    WS->>WS: SetLatch(procLatch)
    Note right of WS: Wake up sender process

    WS->>+WS: WalSndLoop()
    Note right of WS: Main sender processing loop

    WS->>WS: Check WAL availability
    Note right of WS: Determine send range

    WS->>WS: XLogSendPhysical()
    Note right of WS: Prepare WAL data for transmission

    WS->>BUF: WALRead(startptr, count, tli)
    Note right of BUF: Read WAL from buffers/disk

    BUF-->>WS: Return WAL data

    WS->>WS: Construct CopyData message
    Note right of WS: Frame WAL data with protocol headers

    WS->>+NET: pq_putmessage_noblock()
    Note right of NET: Non-blocking network transmission

    NET->>NET: Send to standby

    NET-->>-WS: Transmission complete

    WS->>WS: Update sentPtr
    Note right of WS: Track sent position

    %% Feedback Reception
    NET->>+WS: Standby reply message
    Note left of NET: Async feedback from standby

    WS->>WS: ProcessRepliesIfAny()
    Note right of WS: Non-blocking reply processing

    WS->>WS: ProcessStandbyReplyMessage()
    Note right of WS: Update standby positions

    WS->>WS: Update MyWalSnd state
    Note right of WS: write, flush, apply positions

    WS->>WS: SyncRepReleaseWaiters()
    Note right of WS: Wake synchronous commit waiters

    WS-->>-NET: Process complete

    WS-->>-WS: Continue loop

    %% Performance Optimization Paths
    Note over WAL,WS: Group Commit Optimization
    WAL->>WAL: Group multiple commits
    Note right of WAL: Batch fsync operations

    Note over WS,NET: Transmission Batching
    WS->>WS: Accumulate WAL records
    Note right of WS: Batch transmission for efficiency

    WS->>NET: Send larger messages
    Note right of NET: Reduce network round-trips

    Note over T,NET: End Primary WAL Flow